                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54e129dc-eef5-3be3-99c0-1292ebff2124",
                                        "entry_id": "ca4e098a-fa4f-38fc-b36d-a1a5673c79f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of jinn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c3b108c-dd6b-49e6-af95-8e3e0e4214c6",
                                                "sense_id": "54e129dc-eef5-3be3-99c0-1292ebff2124",
                                                "text": "Necromancy meant originally the conjuring up the souls of the dead, and later included the conjuring of all sorts of inhuman spirits such as sylphs, giants, and djinn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4b91364-7a0b-466b-a85f-a88ada10c91a",
                                                "sense_id": "54e129dc-eef5-3be3-99c0-1292ebff2124",
                                                "text": "I would have liked to know whether he thought this was due to the climate, the diet, or simply malefic djinns."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fdc955a9-04d9-4fc0-866b-85b1f6837ce6",
                        "source_entry_id": "8faea4b5-5dd7-372b-857a-a312c2b70001",
                        "source_sense_id": "7ac21a73-434c-3935-9e31-e93bbdffc2a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "jinn",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jinn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f9d6279-ca4b-3d71-a78d-7534ae3d1198",
                                        "entry_id": "ff436c2a-4dff-319a-9132-bbffdbd46dd2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A human-like spiritual or immaterial being, as opposed to al-ins (people), often invisible but able to manifest in form and also inhabit people or animals; origin of the genie of Western literature, film etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a26e3c26-b3e2-426d-a65e-09b3493aef13",
                                                "sense_id": "7f9d6279-ca4b-3d71-a78d-7534ae3d1198",
                                                "text": "Even the sad jinn within the graven image slept[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dfed923b-fc70-3b2e-bd28-6048f49379fd",
                                        "entry_id": "ff436c2a-4dff-319a-9132-bbffdbd46dd2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Such beings collectively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93336b88-f7b8-4e99-bcc9-7d9ff7e1b477",
                                                "sense_id": "dfed923b-fc70-3b2e-bd28-6048f49379fd",
                                                "text": "There not only jewels but also dangerous jinn abide: the inconvenient or resisted psychological powers that we have not thought or dared to integrate into our lives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a33c336d-e783-4248-83f6-8bcb65ddf142",
                                                "sense_id": "dfed923b-fc70-3b2e-bd28-6048f49379fd",
                                                "text": "Surah 18:50: 'And We told the Angels \"prostrate yourselves before Adam\". So they all prostrated themselves, except Iblees who was one of the jinn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22c7c976-afef-42f5-a637-d7bf43a70d11",
                                                "sense_id": "dfed923b-fc70-3b2e-bd28-6048f49379fd",
                                                "text": "The second context in which jinn occurs in the Qur'an is where we find both ins and jinn are mentioned together. Ins is a collective noun signifying humans, recognisable familiar human beings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
